# Source: https://github.com/lh3/minimap2/issues/738
# Symptom: BED12 record produced by minimap2 splice2bed (paftools.js) with a
#   zero-length middle block; arises when CIGAR contains two consecutive N
#   (intron-skip) operations separated only by an I (insertion): ...N I N...
#   causes the insertion to be skipped without advancing the position. The
#   spec does not forbid blockSize=0, but the offsets are also wrong: the
#   last block runs past chromEnd, which hts-specs §1.9 disallows ("last
#   block must end at chromEnd"). biovalid rejects on the span mismatch.
chr5	140807067	140884662	read1	0	-	140807067	140884662	0	3	422,0,1242	0,75497,77595
chr5	180549000	180730000	read2	0	+	180549000	180730000	0	3	37,0,500	0,37,180963
